1
00:01:27,717 --> 00:01:29,086
Thank you.

2
00:01:45,970 --> 00:01:47,772
Mommy!

3
00:02:03,486 --> 00:02:05,056
Do you know who this is?

4
00:02:05,089 --> 00:02:07,657
Hi, Lily. I'm your mom.

5
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:12,029
Welcome home.

6
00:02:12,063 --> 00:02:13,965
Mommy,
you have to see what I made.

7
00:02:13,998 --> 00:02:16,033
What? What did you make?

8
00:02:16,067 --> 00:02:17,935
Look, it's a two-way radio.

9
00:02:18,803 --> 00:02:21,939
- You did this all by yourself?
- Mmm-hmm.

10
00:02:21,973 --> 00:02:26,143
It still needs work before I'll be
able to talk to you in Afghanistan.

11
00:02:26,177 --> 00:02:30,614
I never would have been able to do that
at your age. It's very impressive, Tommy.

12
00:02:30,647 --> 00:02:31,949
I'll put this in your room.

13
00:02:52,036 --> 00:02:54,038
Those scars say
a lot about you.

14
00:02:54,839 --> 00:02:56,374
What?

15
00:02:56,406 --> 00:02:59,977
That I went to war a doctor and came
back a soldier, like you said I would?

16
00:03:01,946 --> 00:03:03,513
No. Don't.

17
00:03:07,785 --> 00:03:11,588
You know, most of them are on your
front, not on the back.

18
00:03:13,690 --> 00:03:16,127
It tells me my wife
was always facing danger.

19
00:03:17,594 --> 00:03:18,896
She never ran away.

20
00:03:20,597 --> 00:03:22,033
Tells me you're a hero.

21
00:03:23,500 --> 00:03:25,468
Is that really how you feel
about me now?

22
00:03:26,703 --> 00:03:28,672
I'm a hero?

23
00:03:28,705 --> 00:03:30,942
For going to war after
giving birth to our baby girl.

24
00:03:33,543 --> 00:03:35,012
That fight we had...

25
00:03:37,714 --> 00:03:39,749
Whoa. You've never done
that before.

26
00:03:39,784 --> 00:03:41,052
Sorry.

27
00:03:43,586 --> 00:03:45,189
But I didn't say,
I don't like it.

28
00:04:06,110 --> 00:04:07,577
<i>Emily?</i>

29
00:04:10,781 --> 00:04:12,515
<i>Did you fight in the war?</i>

30
00:06:33,958 --> 00:06:35,658
Hey, Love. You okay?

31
00:06:37,194 --> 00:06:38,295
What's this?

32
00:06:40,164 --> 00:06:43,733
It's Tiki Totem.
Brought it back from Hawaii.

33
00:06:43,767 --> 00:06:45,769
The natives believe
that it brings good luck.

34
00:06:48,772 --> 00:06:50,207
Hello there.

35
00:06:54,845 --> 00:06:55,846
Hey.

36
00:06:56,947 --> 00:06:58,115
She has your eyes.

37
00:06:59,783 --> 00:07:02,153
I'll give you two
a minute, okay.

38
00:07:02,186 --> 00:07:04,889
Hey, bye-bye.

39
00:07:04,922 --> 00:07:06,357
Bye-bye.

40
00:07:08,058 --> 00:07:10,194
Hey, let's get you into bed.

41
00:07:21,738 --> 00:07:23,140
Tommy, what are you doing here?

42
00:07:23,174 --> 00:07:24,975
Just watching over Lily, Mom.

43
00:07:26,243 --> 00:07:27,845
Come, I'll tuck you into bed.

44
00:07:27,878 --> 00:07:30,147
You should read
Daddy's book about Hawaii.

45
00:07:30,181 --> 00:07:32,349
He never shares his work
with me until he's done.

46
00:07:32,383 --> 00:07:34,151
Then don't tell him about it.

47
00:07:34,185 --> 00:07:36,787
He keeps it in his study
behind his new book.

48
00:07:36,820 --> 00:07:39,156
- He's writing a new book?
- A book for children.

49
00:07:40,457 --> 00:07:42,159
Come, let's get you to bed.

50
00:07:56,473 --> 00:07:59,376
I'm sure we can still get you to
your piano class in time, Emma.

51
00:07:59,410 --> 00:08:00,511
I'm not playing piano anymore.

52
00:08:00,544 --> 00:08:03,746
- What? But you used to love...
- Oh, you know teenagers.

53
00:08:03,781 --> 00:08:04,982
Love the things
they used to hate,

54
00:08:05,015 --> 00:08:06,817
hate the things
they used to love.

55
00:08:06,850 --> 00:08:07,952
Including us.

56
00:08:07,985 --> 00:08:09,853
Uh, look,
we can just take the bus.

57
00:08:09,887 --> 00:08:12,856
- I'm sure, it's nothing.
- Well, I'm pretty sure, it is.

58
00:08:52,463 --> 00:08:54,398
So, that's where my wrench went.

59
00:08:56,367 --> 00:08:57,968
How about you help me out
with the car?

60
00:09:00,337 --> 00:09:03,173
- Still working on that radio?
- It's much better now.

61
00:09:03,207 --> 00:09:05,309
I talk to Daddy
when he's asleep.

62
00:09:11,015 --> 00:09:13,284
How is that even possible?

63
00:09:13,317 --> 00:09:16,987
Tommy, having an imagination is one thing.
Lying is quite another.

64
00:09:17,021 --> 00:09:21,058
Tesla said, one day we'll be able to
talk to people in other dimensions.

65
00:09:21,091 --> 00:09:22,860
How about you hand me
that wrench?

66
00:09:24,962 --> 00:09:26,997
Tom, could you grab
an extension too?

67
00:09:27,031 --> 00:09:28,132
Sure, be right back.

68
00:09:49,053 --> 00:09:52,189
Tom. Stop playing games.
You're wasting water!

69
00:10:54,952 --> 00:10:55,953
Bee!

70
00:11:01,592 --> 00:11:03,293
It's okay. It's okay.

71
00:11:10,467 --> 00:11:12,069
Where does Dad keep
your EpiPen?

72
00:11:26,417 --> 00:11:30,320
You okay?

73
00:11:30,354 --> 00:11:32,623
<i>Emergency services,
which service do you require?</i>

74
00:11:32,656 --> 00:11:36,260
Hi, hi, I have an emergency.
My son's allergic to bees and he's just...

75
00:11:36,293 --> 00:11:38,495
I'm fine, Mommy.
You don't have to take me.

76
00:11:38,529 --> 00:11:41,265
Just a second. Tommy,
you need to go to the hospital.

77
00:11:41,298 --> 00:11:43,634
Last time it happened,
Dad didn't take me.

78
00:11:44,001 --> 00:11:45,335
He didn't?

79
00:11:48,372 --> 00:11:51,708
- Uh, nev-never mind, so-sorry.
- <i>Okay.</i>

80
00:11:55,546 --> 00:11:57,281
You'll tell me
if you feel strange, right?

81
00:11:58,015 --> 00:11:59,082
Okay.

82
00:12:01,685 --> 00:12:03,086
Uh...

83
00:12:03,654 --> 00:12:05,556
Tommy.

84
00:12:05,589 --> 00:12:08,625
Did you notice any sound
of water in the garage just now?

85
00:12:12,463 --> 00:12:15,332
I want to show you Dad's work
before he comes back from town.

86
00:12:15,365 --> 00:12:16,801
Tommy,
that's called snooping.

87
00:12:16,835 --> 00:12:20,137
It's called having an interest in
what your parents do for a living!

88
00:12:42,426 --> 00:12:44,695
Do you know that demons
can enter people?

89
00:12:50,167 --> 00:12:53,203
This is a Mujina.
A woman without a face.

90
00:12:53,237 --> 00:12:54,806
Dad says her name is Akela.

91
00:12:54,839 --> 00:12:58,208
Tommy. I'm not sure how comfortable I
am with us messing up your dad's study.

92
00:12:58,242 --> 00:13:01,345
I'll do it quickly to relieve you of
your discomfort as soon as possible!

93
00:13:17,094 --> 00:13:18,595
These are the Night Marchers.

94
00:13:18,629 --> 00:13:21,231
One look into their eyes
can suck you in forever.

95
00:13:46,490 --> 00:13:47,724
Spells.

96
00:13:48,860 --> 00:13:51,295
See, a whole book
filled with chants.

97
00:13:52,696 --> 00:13:54,799
A kahuna did one on me
to protect me!

98
00:14:00,170 --> 00:14:02,139
Scary stuff, isn't it?

99
00:14:03,875 --> 00:14:06,343
And if you look at that,

100
00:14:06,376 --> 00:14:09,246
you can't really blame me for wanting to
write something for children, can you?

101
00:14:11,148 --> 00:14:12,716
Tommy, could I have a moment
with your dad please?

102
00:14:25,729 --> 00:14:28,498
Ethan, you're a professor at
Oxford commissioned to explore

103
00:14:28,532 --> 00:14:31,803
the early Polynesian history
of the Hawaiian culture, I mean,

104
00:14:31,836 --> 00:14:34,104
why the sudden interest
of writing children books?

105
00:14:35,505 --> 00:14:36,908
Look at all this.

106
00:14:36,941 --> 00:14:39,276
I mean, all these things!

107
00:14:39,309 --> 00:14:42,379
They're just
things to you and me.

108
00:14:42,412 --> 00:14:44,648
We call them
what the natives call them,

109
00:14:44,681 --> 00:14:48,820
at the end of the day, it's just
stuff we're interested in.

110
00:14:48,853 --> 00:14:52,155
And we study it
like we dissect insects.

111
00:14:52,689 --> 00:14:54,391
Look.

112
00:14:54,424 --> 00:14:56,526
This is Mali.

113
00:14:56,560 --> 00:14:59,329
I met her on my research trip
to Hawaii.

114
00:14:59,363 --> 00:15:05,903
I pretended to believe her when
she told me what she believed in.

115
00:15:05,937 --> 00:15:09,606
I sucked all her most
intimate stories out of her,

116
00:15:09,640 --> 00:15:13,410
for what,
to sell it to the world.

117
00:15:13,443 --> 00:15:17,581
Making people care about how she sees
the world. What's wrong with that?

118
00:15:17,614 --> 00:15:20,617
I'm making the whole world
want to visit Hawaii,

119
00:15:20,651 --> 00:15:25,188
and then turn whatever makes her special
into some cheap tourist attractions.

120
00:15:25,222 --> 00:15:26,824
That's what's wrong.

121
00:15:26,858 --> 00:15:28,558
I want to go back.

122
00:15:28,592 --> 00:15:30,327
I want to return
all the artefacts.

123
00:15:32,897 --> 00:15:36,633
Maybe it'll be good
for you too, good for us.

124
00:15:36,667 --> 00:15:38,635
We could turn it
into a family holiday.

125
00:15:40,537 --> 00:15:42,239
You've never exploited anyone.

126
00:15:45,910 --> 00:15:48,211
I only just got back.

127
00:15:48,245 --> 00:15:50,213
- I missed it.
- I know.

128
00:16:22,847 --> 00:16:24,214
Tommy, what are you doing?

129
00:16:25,783 --> 00:16:28,920
Doing the spell to protect me
against bad things happening.

130
00:16:28,953 --> 00:16:31,488
The one the kahuna taught me.

131
00:16:31,521 --> 00:16:33,825
Nothing bad's going to
happen to you.

132
00:16:33,858 --> 00:16:35,459
I'm here to protect you.

133
00:16:36,928 --> 00:16:38,763
I love you.

134
00:16:38,796 --> 00:16:40,297
Come on, let's go
get something to eat.

135
00:16:44,936 --> 00:16:47,704
<i>Did you know
that demons can enter people?</i>

136
00:17:12,797 --> 00:17:14,899
We need to talk about Tommy.

137
00:17:14,932 --> 00:17:16,768
- I'm worried about him.
- Mmm-hmm.

138
00:18:19,496 --> 00:18:21,398
Forgive me for being crude,

139
00:18:22,532 --> 00:18:23,700
but you're not crazy, you know.

140
00:18:24,701 --> 00:18:25,803
Excuse me?

141
00:18:28,105 --> 00:18:29,406
Here's my card.

142
00:18:31,142 --> 00:18:32,676
Don't let them know,
I've given that to you.

143
00:18:32,709 --> 00:18:37,347
It's bad for business, if patients
realize they're not "patients" after all.

144
00:18:40,084 --> 00:18:41,085
But...

145
00:18:44,889 --> 00:18:46,623
There is something...

146
00:18:47,859 --> 00:18:51,595
ominous that surrounds
your home.

147
00:18:53,865 --> 00:18:57,701
Ah. Give me a ring
when that makes sense to you.

148
00:19:12,482 --> 00:19:14,752
Mrs. Cormack,
the doctor will see you now.

149
00:20:58,722 --> 00:21:01,192
Izzy, what are you doing?

150
00:21:01,225 --> 00:21:04,195
I came back from the doctor
and found this.

151
00:21:04,228 --> 00:21:06,897
- I want to know, who did it and why...
- Tommy.

152
00:21:07,731 --> 00:21:09,266
It was Tommy.

153
00:21:09,300 --> 00:21:11,268
He did it,
just before you got back.

154
00:21:11,969 --> 00:21:13,771
What? Why?

155
00:21:13,804 --> 00:21:15,906
I don't know.
Maybe, he's just looking for attention.

156
00:21:16,941 --> 00:21:18,042
Tommy?

157
00:21:21,078 --> 00:21:22,947
Tommy, did you turn
these photographs around?

158
00:21:24,949 --> 00:21:26,516
I'm getting
to the bottom of this.

159
00:21:32,323 --> 00:21:33,656
All right, Tommy let's go.

160
00:24:17,788 --> 00:24:21,492
I remember the first time you told
me you wanted to play the piano.

161
00:24:21,525 --> 00:24:25,062
We went to this shopping center and there was
a pianist playing in the clothing department.

162
00:24:27,198 --> 00:24:29,333
You stopped and asked
if we could stay and listen.

163
00:24:30,801 --> 00:24:33,938
I sat with you for 20 minutes.

164
00:24:33,971 --> 00:24:36,840
When he finished playing,
you looked up at me and you said...

165
00:24:36,874 --> 00:24:38,375
"I'm going to
do that too, Mommy."

166
00:24:39,276 --> 00:24:41,245
It was the first time
you called me Mom.

167
00:24:42,513 --> 00:24:43,847
Do you remember?

168
00:24:50,988 --> 00:24:52,856
Emma!

169
00:24:52,890 --> 00:24:54,391
Emma, what have you done!

170
00:24:55,259 --> 00:24:56,427
Ethan!

171
00:24:58,095 --> 00:24:59,263
Ethan!

172
00:25:01,065 --> 00:25:03,300
- Izzy.
- Dial the ambulance.

173
00:25:03,334 --> 00:25:05,336
What, what's the matter?

174
00:25:05,936 --> 00:25:07,238
Wha-wha...

175
00:25:10,874 --> 00:25:12,443
Where's Emma?

176
00:25:13,844 --> 00:25:16,780
No. No.
Call the ambulance.

177
00:25:16,814 --> 00:25:18,748
Izzy, but what happened?
What's going on?

178
00:25:19,016 --> 00:25:20,117
Emma.

179
00:25:23,554 --> 00:25:25,055
Emma.

180
00:25:29,460 --> 00:25:30,995
Emma.

181
00:25:34,531 --> 00:25:35,799
Emma.

182
00:25:37,034 --> 00:25:38,902
Where's Emma?

183
00:25:38,936 --> 00:25:41,872
She's at her mom's,
I left you a note.

184
00:25:41,905 --> 00:25:44,475
No, you didn't.
She hates staying there.

185
00:25:44,508 --> 00:25:46,343
Okay, she didn't want me
to tell you.

186
00:25:47,011 --> 00:25:48,946
Where is Emma?

187
00:25:48,979 --> 00:25:51,582
- She's staying at a friend's house.
- No. No!

188
00:25:51,615 --> 00:25:53,984
- She's almost 18, we...
- No! It's not that!

189
00:25:54,018 --> 00:25:55,252
Look, I'll show you, come!

190
00:25:56,854 --> 00:25:59,023
It's all on camera, look.

191
00:26:15,973 --> 00:26:17,174
And?

192
00:26:19,209 --> 00:26:21,312
Emma was there,
I was talking to her.

193
00:26:22,046 --> 00:26:23,113
What's that?

194
00:26:26,317 --> 00:26:28,385
Well, that's just the light
from the window.

195
00:26:34,358 --> 00:26:35,993
The...

196
00:26:36,026 --> 00:26:38,195
The piano,
you heard the piano, right?

197
00:26:41,498 --> 00:26:44,401
- You're lying to me!
- Izzy, Izzy...

198
00:26:44,435 --> 00:26:47,338
Why don't you tell me
what happened to you in Marjah.

199
00:26:47,371 --> 00:26:49,039
It has nothing to do with that!

200
00:26:50,407 --> 00:26:53,210
- Are you taking your pills?
- Yes.

201
00:26:53,243 --> 00:26:55,346
- And it wasn't a hallucination.
- Listen to me.

202
00:26:55,379 --> 00:26:58,148
Why don't we take that family
holiday I've been talking about?

203
00:26:58,182 --> 00:27:00,217
I really think a short break
will do you good.

204
00:27:00,250 --> 00:27:03,120
I'm not stressed, Ethan.
The doctor said...

205
00:27:04,655 --> 00:27:05,956
Did you see that?

206
00:27:06,990 --> 00:27:07,991
There.

207
00:27:16,066 --> 00:27:18,268
It's just Tommy.

208
00:27:18,302 --> 00:27:19,970
And you look
pretty stressed to me.

209
00:27:40,391 --> 00:27:41,558
See.

210
00:27:44,495 --> 00:27:46,463
I'm not leaving
till I figure this out.

211
00:27:52,035 --> 00:27:53,170
Okay.

212
00:28:17,461 --> 00:28:19,229
<i>Hello, Elizabeth.</i>

213
00:28:19,263 --> 00:28:21,131
How did you know
it was me calling?

214
00:28:23,033 --> 00:28:24,535
<i>I sense it's an emergency.</i>

215
00:28:31,708 --> 00:28:32,877
You can set up in here.

216
00:28:32,911 --> 00:28:36,346
Uh, may I ask that we get
the formalities out of the way?

217
00:28:36,380 --> 00:28:37,849
Listen, my husband believes

218
00:28:37,882 --> 00:28:40,350
it's easier to indulge in the eternal
after completing material matters.

219
00:28:40,384 --> 00:28:41,485
Oh, of course.

220
00:28:42,686 --> 00:28:44,521
- Thank you.
- Um, hello?

221
00:28:44,555 --> 00:28:47,691
Ethan, I asked Richard to
come here to perform a seance.

222
00:28:47,724 --> 00:28:49,660
Uh. Good afternoon.
I'm Richard Turner, this is Hugh...

223
00:28:49,693 --> 00:28:51,562
Mmm-hmm. Yeah.
Can I speak to you for a moment?

224
00:28:51,595 --> 00:28:54,164
Sure. I'll be right back.

225
00:28:58,602 --> 00:29:00,471
- Who are these people?
- Look...

226
00:29:02,172 --> 00:29:03,674
I met Richard
at the psychologist's office,

227
00:29:03,707 --> 00:29:07,177
and he just understood what was wrong
with me without me saying anything.

228
00:29:07,211 --> 00:29:09,379
And then,
and then I called him,

229
00:29:09,413 --> 00:29:11,148
and he knew we needed help.

230
00:29:11,181 --> 00:29:15,686
So, this stalker is hitting on women with
mental problems in a psychologist's office?

231
00:29:15,719 --> 00:29:18,622
It's so unlike you to be jealous
and Richard's gay.

232
00:29:20,825 --> 00:29:23,627
Look, I know this
doesn't make much sense to you

233
00:29:23,660 --> 00:29:25,429
and to be quite frank,
it doesn't make much sense to me...

234
00:29:25,462 --> 00:29:27,631
No, no, it makes perfect sense.

235
00:29:27,664 --> 00:29:28,833
Don't you see?

236
00:29:28,867 --> 00:29:32,369
He pays the receptionist
to get information on patients.

237
00:29:32,402 --> 00:29:35,439
He puts your number in his phone
and he knows when you're calling.

238
00:29:35,472 --> 00:29:38,609
Then he sells you some
whack-job spiritual mumbo jumbo.

239
00:29:38,642 --> 00:29:41,512
Look, I'm not asking you to understand,
but I just want you to respect...

240
00:29:41,545 --> 00:29:43,347
- I'm getting these people out of my house.
- No.

241
00:29:43,380 --> 00:29:45,249
I went to see
a psychologist for you.

242
00:29:45,282 --> 00:29:47,584
Now this is for me,
and you will respect that.

243
00:29:49,686 --> 00:29:51,255
I'm taking
the children to a hotel.

244
00:29:51,288 --> 00:29:53,156
Come on, Ethan,
you're overreacting.

245
00:29:53,190 --> 00:29:55,259
What, I'm overreacting?

246
00:29:55,292 --> 00:29:58,328
Ever since you've been back,
you've been a disaster.

247
00:29:58,362 --> 00:30:00,097
And I'm overreacting?

248
00:30:01,331 --> 00:30:03,400
Emma? Tommy!

249
00:30:08,272 --> 00:30:09,606
- I do apologize.
- Please.

250
00:30:09,640 --> 00:30:12,777
No need for apologies.
This can be very difficult for a family.

251
00:30:12,810 --> 00:30:14,578
Please, sit.

252
00:30:14,611 --> 00:30:19,349
I will try to communicate,
what I can to you.

253
00:30:19,383 --> 00:30:22,085
Please feel free to ask
any questions whilst I'm in it.

254
00:30:22,887 --> 00:30:24,187
In what?

255
00:30:25,757 --> 00:30:27,524
You'll see.

256
00:30:27,558 --> 00:30:30,227
Hugh will be recording
everything from here.

257
00:30:30,260 --> 00:30:32,797
This night-vision camera
can detect ectoplasm,

258
00:30:32,830 --> 00:30:36,133
the substance astral bodies
leave behind.

259
00:30:36,166 --> 00:30:38,135
And our white noise machine
catches frequencies

260
00:30:38,168 --> 00:30:39,436
humans have a hard time hearing.

261
00:30:44,308 --> 00:30:47,678
Sometimes we find something,
but it's not a sure thing.

262
00:30:48,745 --> 00:30:51,081
Just remember,
whatever happens...

263
00:30:52,249 --> 00:30:53,617
stay calm.

264
00:30:54,618 --> 00:30:56,720
Stay seated.

265
00:30:57,855 --> 00:31:01,158
Do not attempt to make
physical contact with a spirit.

266
00:31:01,859 --> 00:31:03,594
It is not safe.

267
00:31:31,321 --> 00:31:33,290
Someone is here.

268
00:31:37,561 --> 00:31:39,262
A... A woman.

269
00:31:44,936 --> 00:31:47,170
A woman who lived here.

270
00:31:47,204 --> 00:31:48,773
She is attached to this place.

271
00:31:50,674 --> 00:31:52,275
What does she want?

272
00:31:53,945 --> 00:31:56,446
Something's bothering her.

273
00:31:56,480 --> 00:31:58,649
Something's wrong.
She wants...

274
00:31:58,682 --> 00:31:59,884
What is it?

275
00:32:04,856 --> 00:32:05,857
Are you okay?

276
00:32:21,906 --> 00:32:24,241
The demon's inside!

277
00:33:11,588 --> 00:33:13,290
There is a presence here.

278
00:33:15,927 --> 00:33:17,327
What does it want?

279
00:33:17,962 --> 00:33:19,429
Something dark.

280
00:33:21,799 --> 00:33:23,500
Your family is in great danger.

281
00:33:26,838 --> 00:33:28,538
This house needs
a proper cleansing.

282
00:33:30,775 --> 00:33:32,542
Can you... Can you do it?

283
00:33:32,576 --> 00:33:33,744
He needs to rest.

284
00:33:35,746 --> 00:33:37,815
- Oh, thank you.
- We'll have to come back another day.

285
00:33:53,765 --> 00:33:56,433
- Ethan, Ethan, I have proof that I...
- <i>Yeah?</i>

286
00:33:57,969 --> 00:33:59,369
<i>What? Izzy?</i>

287
00:33:59,837 --> 00:34:00,938
<i>What?</i>

288
00:34:05,408 --> 00:34:06,309
What...

289
00:34:06,343 --> 00:34:07,879
<i>Come on, Izzy,
what is this?</i>

290
00:34:09,446 --> 00:34:11,581
- <i>Huh? You there?</i>
- Huh, yeah.

291
00:34:12,549 --> 00:34:13,785
I'm still here.

292
00:34:15,920 --> 00:34:17,387
Ethan, you were right.

293
00:34:18,756 --> 00:34:20,490
You were right
about everything, I-I...

294
00:34:22,492 --> 00:34:24,028
Please, come back
so we can talk.

295
00:34:25,062 --> 00:34:26,730
I'm such a fool.

296
00:34:48,618 --> 00:34:50,387
We didn't go past
the corner shop.

297
00:34:53,157 --> 00:34:55,492
There's no way I'm gonna
give up on you that easily.

298
00:34:56,626 --> 00:34:58,695
What should I do?

299
00:34:58,728 --> 00:35:01,598
Our bags are packed,
why don't you get yours?

300
00:35:03,034 --> 00:35:04,568
Then we'll go on that holiday.

301
00:36:03,493 --> 00:36:05,629
Emma, can you get the keys
from the postbox?

302
00:36:10,134 --> 00:36:12,636
You'll love it,
it was so great last time.

303
00:36:14,005 --> 00:36:15,605
All right, Tommy?

304
00:36:16,539 --> 00:36:17,808
Home, sweet home.

305
00:36:25,049 --> 00:36:26,549
You can't say it.

306
00:36:26,583 --> 00:36:28,585
- <i>Humu-naka...</i>
- Wrong.

307
00:36:28,618 --> 00:36:30,587
Then you say.

308
00:36:30,620 --> 00:36:32,489
<i>Humuhumunukunukuapua'a.</i>

309
00:36:32,522 --> 00:36:35,059
- You're making that up.
- No, it's a real fish.

310
00:36:35,092 --> 00:36:36,827
I'll show you one in the lagoon.

311
00:36:38,095 --> 00:36:39,529
Fine.

312
00:36:44,001 --> 00:36:46,804
Tommy, why don't you go
with your sister? Could be fun.

313
00:36:52,509 --> 00:36:54,145
I have to walk through the bees.

314
00:36:54,178 --> 00:36:56,680
The bees don't really
come out of the hive.

315
00:36:56,713 --> 00:36:58,149
You can always walk
through the house.

316
00:37:07,657 --> 00:37:09,459
See how high you can go.

317
00:37:10,962 --> 00:37:12,263
Whoa!

318
00:37:14,031 --> 00:37:15,766
Ahhh!

319
00:37:17,634 --> 00:37:18,869
Whoo!

320
00:39:01,138 --> 00:39:02,940
Mommy?

321
00:39:02,973 --> 00:39:04,341
Have you seen my dominoes?

322
00:39:05,976 --> 00:39:08,179
Tommy.

323
00:39:08,212 --> 00:39:10,147
Why did you turn over
those family photographs?

324
00:39:11,248 --> 00:39:12,817
You can tell me...

325
00:39:13,517 --> 00:39:16,787
- I didn't.
- Stop lying to me!

326
00:39:16,821 --> 00:39:18,823
You're keeping secrets from me.

327
00:39:18,856 --> 00:39:21,959
Tell me! What is going on?

328
00:39:21,992 --> 00:39:24,061
Who were you speaking to
at night over the radio?

329
00:39:24,762 --> 00:39:26,063
Huh?

330
00:39:26,097 --> 00:39:28,966
I caught you doing
a chant in your room!

331
00:39:28,999 --> 00:39:32,002
You told me you saw a kahuna and
she did a protection spell on you.

332
00:39:32,036 --> 00:39:33,270
What happened there?

333
00:39:34,972 --> 00:39:36,974
Tell me, it's important, Tommy!

334
00:39:37,975 --> 00:39:39,376
What are you hiding from me?

335
00:39:45,015 --> 00:39:47,151
I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

336
00:39:48,819 --> 00:39:50,254
I'm sorry.

337
00:39:51,688 --> 00:39:53,824
We can talk later.

338
00:39:53,858 --> 00:39:55,893
When you feel better,
okay?

339
00:40:03,334 --> 00:40:05,870
- Hey. Where you going?
- Hey.

340
00:40:08,272 --> 00:40:11,108
Listen, I've been seeing things.

341
00:40:11,142 --> 00:40:13,144
Hallucinations.

342
00:40:13,177 --> 00:40:15,712
And it's not PTSD.
I've been taking the pills.

343
00:40:15,745 --> 00:40:18,816
How can you say it's not PTSD?

344
00:40:18,849 --> 00:40:20,885
That's the only thing
that makes sense.

345
00:40:20,918 --> 00:40:23,454
Tommy told me he saw a kahuna.
I didn't think anything of it at the time,

346
00:40:23,487 --> 00:40:27,224
but maybe she knows what's going on.
Maybe she caused it.

347
00:40:27,258 --> 00:40:30,060
Izzy, you've just came back
from war and you're a...

348
00:40:32,763 --> 00:40:34,064
Finish your sentence.

349
00:40:35,166 --> 00:40:36,800
You're my wife.

350
00:40:36,834 --> 00:40:39,436
So what, because I'm a woman,
it has to be PTSD?

351
00:40:39,470 --> 00:40:40,804
You called me your hero.

352
00:40:40,838 --> 00:40:44,408
And you are, but this has nothing
to do with you being a woman,

353
00:40:44,441 --> 00:40:47,845
and everything to do with
you being who you are.

354
00:40:47,878 --> 00:40:51,882
And don't you see, you run into
danger like it's not gonna hurt you.

355
00:40:51,916 --> 00:40:53,417
That's the thing about war.

356
00:40:53,450 --> 00:40:57,154
It always leaves scars,
and not all of them are physical.

357
00:40:57,188 --> 00:40:59,456
I'm going to find that kahuna.
This is not PTSD!

358
00:40:59,490 --> 00:41:02,860
Okay. Okay.
But she's not open now.

359
00:41:02,893 --> 00:41:05,329
We'll go first thing in the
morning and I'll go with you,

360
00:41:06,764 --> 00:41:09,133
Whatever it is
that's wrong with you,

361
00:41:09,166 --> 00:41:11,035
we'll figure it out as a family.

362
00:41:11,869 --> 00:41:12,870
Come on.

363
00:41:41,432 --> 00:41:43,234
Petey?

364
00:41:50,507 --> 00:41:52,910
Petey, outside, boy.

365
00:42:04,154 --> 00:42:07,024
Petey, outside!

366
00:42:07,057 --> 00:42:10,361
Hey, we left Petey at home
with the dog sitter, remember?

367
00:42:12,062 --> 00:42:13,497
Just go back to sleep, love.

368
00:42:34,918 --> 00:42:36,887
Tommy, what's going on?
Why you up?

369
00:42:37,521 --> 00:42:38,956
Mom?

370
00:42:43,127 --> 00:42:44,795
It's from the kahuna you saw.

371
00:42:46,463 --> 00:42:48,032
We'll go there tomorrow.

372
00:42:49,867 --> 00:42:51,302
Tommy?

373
00:43:08,952 --> 00:43:10,587
It's just
that silly Tiki Totem.

374
00:43:11,355 --> 00:43:12,823
It scares me too.

375
00:43:19,029 --> 00:43:21,298
Can I sleep with you tonight?

376
00:43:23,667 --> 00:43:25,069
Of course, you can.

377
00:43:51,695 --> 00:43:53,497
Oh, morning.

378
00:43:53,530 --> 00:43:56,567
It's my last chance to do some
magic before I return it all.

379
00:43:57,968 --> 00:43:59,169
Don't worry.

380
00:43:59,203 --> 00:44:01,939
Apparently it only works if you
burn specific herbs as well.

381
00:44:02,606 --> 00:44:04,508
- Show me.
- Yeah.

382
00:44:43,447 --> 00:44:45,249
- What's wrong with that boy?
- Mommy.

383
00:44:46,116 --> 00:44:47,151
I'll go see if he's okay.

384
00:44:59,329 --> 00:45:00,364
Tommy, where are we going?

385
00:45:15,145 --> 00:45:16,447
Tommy, where are you
taking me to?

386
00:45:30,227 --> 00:45:31,528
What are we looking at, Tommy?

387
00:45:33,798 --> 00:45:35,566
He says we should
get in the water.

388
00:45:35,800 --> 00:45:37,034
Who?

389
00:45:37,601 --> 00:45:40,370
He said I shouldn't say.

390
00:45:40,404 --> 00:45:43,273
He was saying "Why isn't Emma
afraid of the water anymore?"

391
00:45:45,042 --> 00:45:46,610
Okay, stay here, Tommy.

392
00:46:18,108 --> 00:46:19,376
There's something
pulling me, Tommy.

393
00:46:47,104 --> 00:46:51,408
Ethan, we found three dead bodies
in the lagoon. We need to leave now.

394
00:46:51,441 --> 00:46:53,310
I'll call the police from the car.
You go get Emma.

395
00:47:05,757 --> 00:47:07,057
Emma?

396
00:47:10,460 --> 00:47:12,764
Izzy, have you seen Emma?
I can't find her anywhere.

397
00:47:12,797 --> 00:47:14,164
- Have you looked outside?
- Yeah.

398
00:47:15,767 --> 00:47:18,268
- Emma?
- Emma.

399
00:47:18,302 --> 00:47:20,370
- Emma.
- Emma, darling, we're leaving now.

400
00:47:26,143 --> 00:47:27,779
- Is that a telephone?
- Yeah.

401
00:48:03,781 --> 00:48:06,683
It's the basement.
Stay here and call the police.

402
00:48:53,831 --> 00:48:55,967
- Hello?
- <i>Mommy?</i>

403
00:48:56,000 --> 00:48:58,301
Emma? Emma, where are you?
Are you okay?

404
00:48:58,335 --> 00:49:00,637
<i>Mommy. Please help me.</i>

405
00:49:00,671 --> 00:49:05,475
<i>There's a man. He wants you to follow
the sound of the boiling water.</i>

406
00:49:05,509 --> 00:49:08,946
Emma. Tell me.
What do you see around you?

407
00:49:08,980 --> 00:49:11,448
<i>Do you hear it? Please.</i>

408
00:49:14,418 --> 00:49:15,619
Yes.

409
00:49:17,621 --> 00:49:19,322
- I can hear it.
- <i>Follow it.</i>

410
00:49:36,573 --> 00:49:38,642
I found the boiling water.

411
00:49:38,675 --> 00:49:43,714
<i>The man says there is a table.
He wants you to tie yourself to the table.</i>

412
00:49:43,747 --> 00:49:47,350
Emma. Tell me what
do you see around you?

413
00:49:47,384 --> 00:49:51,254
<i>Please, Mommy. He's hurting me.
Tie yourself to the table.</i>

414
00:49:51,288 --> 00:49:53,290
Tell that man
that I want to speak to him.

415
00:49:53,323 --> 00:49:54,658
<i>He's hurting me.</i>

416
00:49:54,691 --> 00:49:58,662
Tell him I won't follow his
instructions until I speak to him.

417
00:49:59,931 --> 00:50:02,800
Emma? Emma, are you still there?

418
00:50:16,446 --> 00:50:19,851
What's wrong with you?
Get that mask off.

419
00:50:19,884 --> 00:50:21,318
I've seen it
in your dad's office.

420
00:50:24,055 --> 00:50:26,423
Just wanted to see
how much you really love me.

421
00:50:26,456 --> 00:50:29,794
- If you would put your own life in danger to save mine.
- Of course, I would.

422
00:50:29,827 --> 00:50:32,729
Yet, you didn't tie
yourself to the table.

423
00:50:32,764 --> 00:50:35,066
Emma, something terrible has
happened here and we need to go.

424
00:50:35,099 --> 00:50:36,801
Tie yourself to the table.

425
00:50:36,834 --> 00:50:38,635
Prove that you love me.
That you trust me.

426
00:50:40,004 --> 00:50:41,338
I'm not taking any of this.

427
00:50:42,639 --> 00:50:43,740
We're going now.

428
00:50:48,045 --> 00:50:50,848
Why are you still making breakfast?
Did you call the police?

429
00:50:52,850 --> 00:50:56,653
Uh, yeah. Of course. They're on their way.
But you found Emma.

430
00:51:02,425 --> 00:51:05,062
She was never in any real danger.
All right, we're leaving this place now.

431
00:51:05,096 --> 00:51:07,430
You tell your daughter to get her
stuff and I'm going to get Tommy.

432
00:51:25,950 --> 00:51:27,952
<i>Tommy? Tommy?</i>

433
00:51:27,985 --> 00:51:29,486
- <i>Can you hear me?</i>
- I can hear you.

434
00:51:30,620 --> 00:51:33,090
Tommy, we're going.

435
00:51:33,124 --> 00:51:36,459
- Daddy wants to talk to you.
- I just saw your daddy. He's downstairs.

436
00:51:36,493 --> 00:51:37,494
<i>Izzy?</i>

437
00:51:38,129 --> 00:51:39,462
<i>That's not me.</i>

438
00:51:43,733 --> 00:51:47,504
<i>You need to take Tommy
and leave immediately.</i>

439
00:51:47,537 --> 00:51:50,908
- What about Emma?
- That's not her either.

440
00:51:50,942 --> 00:51:54,779
- Last time we were here...
- <i>The family from the lagoon took our bodies.</i>

441
00:51:54,812 --> 00:51:58,015
- And they want yours too.
- That's not possible.

442
00:51:58,049 --> 00:52:00,417
<i>I tried to warn you.
The pictures on the wall.</i>

443
00:52:02,053 --> 00:52:05,056
<i>The piano,
and the baby monitor.</i>

444
00:52:07,792 --> 00:52:09,626
<i>We tried to scare you
away from this place.</i>

445
00:52:14,899 --> 00:52:16,801
Why didn't you tell me before?

446
00:52:16,834 --> 00:52:20,872
I tried. But they make it look
like I can't be trusted.

447
00:52:20,905 --> 00:52:22,940
I didn't turn over
the photographs.

448
00:52:22,974 --> 00:52:25,575
You stopped believing me, Mom.

449
00:52:25,609 --> 00:52:28,779
I told you. I talk to Daddy
when that man's asleep

450
00:52:28,813 --> 00:52:30,547
- and you...
- I'm sorry I didn't believe you, Tommy.

451
00:52:32,515 --> 00:52:33,583
We need to hide.

452
00:52:36,586 --> 00:52:37,621
Maybe in the tunnel.

453
00:52:58,708 --> 00:53:01,979
Please, leave Lily alone.

454
00:53:02,013 --> 00:53:04,048
You have no idea

455
00:53:04,081 --> 00:53:07,450
how I hated talking in your
husband's queer accent.

456
00:53:08,518 --> 00:53:09,552
Oh.

457
00:53:14,624 --> 00:53:15,760
Did you get the chant?

458
00:53:24,035 --> 00:53:26,736
It's our culture
your husband wanted to steal.

459
00:53:26,771 --> 00:53:29,840
So, she took him and Emma
for me and our daughter.

460
00:53:31,508 --> 00:53:33,811
Show army girl here
where to go.

461
00:53:33,844 --> 00:53:35,712
Your mom needs
a new body too.

462
00:53:44,521 --> 00:53:46,023
Let's try this again.

463
00:53:46,057 --> 00:53:47,490
Tie yourself to the table.

464
00:55:08,105 --> 00:55:09,206
She's here.

465
00:57:01,986 --> 00:57:03,020
Emma?

466
00:57:03,888 --> 00:57:04,922
Emma?

467
00:59:03,607 --> 00:59:05,509
Hello?

468
00:59:08,846 --> 00:59:10,147
Hello?

469
00:59:34,972 --> 00:59:36,140
Mommy, can you hear me?

470
00:59:37,241 --> 00:59:38,342
Mommy, follow my voice.

471
01:00:04,101 --> 01:00:05,102
Mommy.

472
01:00:07,571 --> 01:00:10,140
Tommy, please don't speak.

473
01:00:31,295 --> 01:00:33,130
Tommy, can you hear me?

474
01:00:34,298 --> 01:00:35,299
I can hear you.

475
01:00:35,966 --> 01:00:38,202
I need you to go to the kitchen.

476
01:00:38,235 --> 01:00:41,105
There's a door in the pantry
that leads to the basement.

477
01:00:41,138 --> 01:00:42,439
Take the tunnel
and meet me there.

478
01:00:46,710 --> 01:00:48,312
Tommy,

479
01:00:48,345 --> 01:00:50,914
I need your body to fix this.

480
01:00:50,948 --> 01:00:53,217
You're the only one
that can save us.

481
01:00:53,250 --> 01:00:55,285
We need to perform
transference on you.

482
01:00:58,222 --> 01:00:59,223
It's boiling.

483
01:01:03,460 --> 01:01:05,429
I need you
to pour it over your body

484
01:01:06,430 --> 01:01:08,031
from your toes to your face.

485
01:01:10,434 --> 01:01:11,435
Can you do that for me?

486
01:01:14,538 --> 01:01:16,240
Uh...

487
01:01:17,474 --> 01:01:18,475
Tommy,

488
01:01:19,376 --> 01:01:21,478
your whole body.

489
01:01:21,512 --> 01:01:26,083
No matter what happens...
don't stop.

490
01:01:27,351 --> 01:01:28,352
Okay.

491
01:02:25,542 --> 01:02:28,078
Tommy, you stay safe.
Mommy loves you.

492
01:03:04,481 --> 01:03:06,450
Sorry, buddy. You know too much.

493
01:03:08,352 --> 01:03:09,353
You gotta go.

494
01:04:14,852 --> 01:04:16,119
Argh!

495
01:04:34,906 --> 01:04:36,106
Is something burning?

496
01:04:38,675 --> 01:04:40,510
Tommy. The basement.

497
01:05:15,679 --> 01:05:16,613
What are you still doing here?

498
01:05:16,647 --> 01:05:18,248
Open the door, Tommy!

499
01:05:38,468 --> 01:05:39,670
I'm letting you out now!

500
01:05:41,271 --> 01:05:42,706
I'll deal with Tommy.

501
01:06:06,864 --> 01:06:07,865
Go to sleep.

502
01:06:44,035 --> 01:06:45,335
Please let me out.

503
01:06:56,546 --> 01:06:57,982
Tommy, this isn't funny.

504
01:07:01,651 --> 01:07:03,855
Seriously, let me out.

505
01:07:03,888 --> 01:07:05,589
You've come from the house
in the forest

506
01:07:05,622 --> 01:07:06,858
where the road ends.

507
01:07:07,759 --> 01:07:08,760
Tommy!

508
01:07:13,396 --> 01:07:14,564
A woman lived there.

509
01:07:16,934 --> 01:07:18,936
People whispered
she could transfer

510
01:07:18,970 --> 01:07:20,637
the dead into the living.

511
01:07:24,341 --> 01:07:26,343
I sense she was murdered
with her family.

512
01:07:29,947 --> 01:07:33,583
But you've already been
transferred, haven't you?

513
01:07:35,519 --> 01:07:36,788
Tommy!

514
01:07:39,056 --> 01:07:41,691
It's my daughter. Emma.

515
01:07:41,725 --> 01:07:43,828
Tommy, let me out now!

516
01:07:49,366 --> 01:07:51,969
I'm sorry. I cannot help.

517
01:07:55,372 --> 01:07:56,808
You've lost someone, too.

518
01:07:59,043 --> 01:08:00,912
A spirit you cannot get back.

519
01:08:03,580 --> 01:08:04,714
I was in Marjah.

520
01:08:06,416 --> 01:08:10,687
A girl, my son's age,
was wearing an explosive vest.

521
01:08:13,423 --> 01:08:15,059
I shot her
before she could trigger it.

522
01:08:19,663 --> 01:08:22,666
I know what it's like to not be
able to protect the innocent.

523
01:08:24,568 --> 01:08:27,571
But how do you keep them safe
from something you can't see?

524
01:08:32,910 --> 01:08:33,911
You cannot.

525
01:08:37,581 --> 01:08:40,417
But we are going to try. Please.

526
01:08:44,789 --> 01:08:47,524
We must take her back to
where the transference occurred,

527
01:08:48,458 --> 01:08:51,394
call her name. Call her back.

528
01:08:57,434 --> 01:08:58,435
Let's go.

529
01:09:38,575 --> 01:09:39,877
Mama?

530
01:09:40,677 --> 01:09:41,711
Is that you?

531
01:09:43,613 --> 01:09:44,614
They're escaping.

532
01:09:45,016 --> 01:09:46,017
Go.

533
01:10:30,895 --> 01:10:33,630
Tommy, it's your dad.

534
01:10:33,663 --> 01:10:34,664
It's not.

535
01:10:36,599 --> 01:10:37,667
Aunty Mae,

536
01:10:37,701 --> 01:10:40,570
it's time to get my family
back into their bodies.

537
01:11:13,670 --> 01:11:14,671
Did it work?

538
01:11:17,208 --> 01:11:18,209
Tommy.

539
01:11:19,810 --> 01:11:21,912
Tommy, I'm so sorry
I put you through this.

540
01:11:22,579 --> 01:11:23,747
I'm so sorry.

541
01:11:35,192 --> 01:11:36,961
Go and see to her.

542
01:11:36,994 --> 01:11:38,195
I'll bring your husband back.

543
01:12:27,812 --> 01:12:29,612
Tommy, can you make sure
Lily's all right?

544
01:12:34,018 --> 01:12:35,019
Emma?

545
01:12:40,124 --> 01:12:41,292
Emma, are you all right?

546
01:12:46,663 --> 01:12:48,232
You've been lost for so long.

547
01:12:50,201 --> 01:12:51,902
Ever since the last time
you stayed here.

548
01:12:58,309 --> 01:13:00,010
<i>You must be so tired.</i>

549
01:13:03,047 --> 01:13:04,915
<i>It's almost over.</i>

550
01:13:04,949 --> 01:13:06,851
<i>We're getting your dad
into his body now.</i>

551
01:13:07,785 --> 01:13:08,786
<i>I promise.</i>

552
01:13:23,100 --> 01:13:24,101
Izzy?

553
01:13:26,770 --> 01:13:28,239
I missed you so much.

554
01:13:28,272 --> 01:13:29,273
Wait.

555
01:13:30,374 --> 01:13:31,876
The day I left for Marjah,

556
01:13:33,010 --> 01:13:34,178
what did we fight about?

557
01:13:35,212 --> 01:13:36,380
You said you were leaving

558
01:13:36,413 --> 01:13:40,217
to stop the bleeding
of a country in pain.

559
01:13:40,251 --> 01:13:41,886
Even if it meant being apart.

560
01:13:41,919 --> 01:13:43,720
And you said...

561
01:13:43,754 --> 01:13:46,323
That their blood
will taint your hands.

562
01:13:46,357 --> 01:13:49,960
I'm sorry. I'm sorry I left.

563
01:13:49,994 --> 01:13:52,229
No. No, it was me.
I was just being selfish.

564
01:13:53,364 --> 01:13:55,966
The world needs doctors
like you.

565
01:13:56,000 --> 01:13:57,935
Doctors that become soldiers.

566
01:13:57,968 --> 01:13:59,436
Doesn't matter.

567
01:13:59,470 --> 01:14:02,907
Just happy you came back
to save us, too, Captain.

568
01:14:08,245 --> 01:14:10,080
- Come.
- Daddy.

569
01:14:10,114 --> 01:14:12,715
You're back.
You're finally back.

570
01:14:16,954 --> 01:14:18,455
I need to perform a cleansing.

571
01:14:33,037 --> 01:14:34,505
What happened to her?

572
01:14:34,538 --> 01:14:35,839
Kaimoni.

573
01:14:35,873 --> 01:14:37,841
It is a dangerous demon.

574
01:14:37,875 --> 01:14:38,943
Where's Lily?

575
01:14:40,477 --> 01:14:41,845
- Look after Tommy.
- Sure.

576
01:14:57,328 --> 01:14:58,329
Emma.

577
01:15:03,000 --> 01:15:05,502
Please leave Lily alone.

578
01:15:41,605 --> 01:15:43,207
Sounds like she's in her room.

579
01:15:46,210 --> 01:15:48,045
I'll make sure Lily stays safe.

580
01:15:50,547 --> 01:15:51,815
Listen.

581
01:15:55,886 --> 01:15:57,521
- Going to be okay?
- Yes.

582
01:16:09,867 --> 01:16:10,968
That's not Emma.

583
01:16:13,203 --> 01:16:15,506
Last time I saw
the Kaimoni take someone...

584
01:16:16,573 --> 01:16:17,841
it killed her.

585
01:16:18,976 --> 01:16:20,177
I killed her.

586
01:16:21,245 --> 01:16:22,246
No.

587
01:16:22,813 --> 01:16:24,214
You tried to save her.

588
01:16:28,319 --> 01:16:30,854
Her name was Ruby.

589
01:16:30,888 --> 01:16:33,490
I named her after the family
of the plumeria flower.

590
01:16:40,664 --> 01:16:43,033
Transference will not work
on a demon.

591
01:16:44,034 --> 01:16:46,103
A demon has never lived.

592
01:16:48,205 --> 01:16:50,174
I need to perform an exorcism.

593
01:17:04,054 --> 01:17:05,055
Emma?

594
01:17:45,529 --> 01:17:48,198
Please make it stop.

595
01:18:02,346 --> 01:18:04,581
Make it stop! Make it stop!

596
01:18:21,632 --> 01:18:23,434
The demon is too strong.

597
01:18:25,169 --> 01:18:28,038
The lagoon.
We must take her there.

598
01:18:29,006 --> 01:18:30,174
We need to kill it.

599
01:18:58,735 --> 01:19:00,103
Put her under.

600
01:20:35,699 --> 01:20:36,700
Emma!

601
01:20:37,769 --> 01:20:38,836
Izzy, stop!

602
01:20:41,238 --> 01:20:42,639
It will take her again.

603
01:20:52,316 --> 01:20:54,117
Take me instead.

604
01:20:54,151 --> 01:20:55,652
This girl, you will not hurt.

605
01:20:55,686 --> 01:20:57,789
- No, let me go.
- No.

606
01:20:57,822 --> 01:20:59,757
This is my fight. Not yours.

607
01:20:59,791 --> 01:21:02,659
You need to stay with your
family and keep them safe.

608
01:21:02,693 --> 01:21:04,161
That is your purpose.

609
01:22:25,843 --> 01:22:27,711
She's gone. It's too late.

610
01:22:27,744 --> 01:22:29,312
No. She can still come back.

611
01:22:36,821 --> 01:22:38,255
Izzy, Izzy...

612
01:22:45,495 --> 01:22:48,298
I can't remember.
What did she say?

613
01:22:48,331 --> 01:22:49,599
Just use your own words.

614
01:22:54,638 --> 01:22:56,974
I should've been here.
I'm sorry I wasn't there.

615
01:23:01,378 --> 01:23:02,479
Please.

616
01:23:03,647 --> 01:23:05,382
Please, God, bring her back.

617
01:23:05,415 --> 01:23:08,385
Bring my little girl back.
Don't let another innocent die.

618
01:23:09,020 --> 01:23:10,287
Please.

619
01:23:17,494 --> 01:23:18,763
- Mommy?
- Emma.

620
01:23:20,031 --> 01:23:21,231
Emma?

621
01:23:24,501 --> 01:23:26,403
Wait.

622
01:23:26,436 --> 01:23:28,472
What happened
on your 13th birthday?

623
01:23:28,505 --> 01:23:30,440
I tripped and had to get
a cast on my leg,

624
01:23:30,474 --> 01:23:34,011
but I didn't mind because
I could still play the piano.

625
01:23:34,045 --> 01:23:37,347
And, when I took you to your first
swimming class, what did you tell me?

626
01:23:37,380 --> 01:23:39,483
That I'm allergic
to water.

627
01:23:44,721 --> 01:23:47,759
I missed you...
I missed you so, so much.

628
01:23:52,429 --> 01:23:53,865
And Auntie Mae?

629
01:24:25,495 --> 01:24:27,799
How about we open that restaurant
we always talked about?

630
01:24:27,832 --> 01:24:30,768
The one that only serves
home-brewed beers?

631
01:24:30,802 --> 01:24:32,302
With home-cooked meals.

632
01:24:44,514 --> 01:24:45,850
Mom?

633
01:24:45,883 --> 01:24:47,350
Does this mean you'll stay?

634
01:24:47,384 --> 01:24:48,518
Mmm-hmm.

635
01:24:57,962 --> 01:25:00,064
Then this is just lovely.

636
01:25:00,097 --> 01:25:02,767
Best pie I've ever had.
Just lovely.

637
01:25:23,141 --> 01:25:28,141
Subtitles by explosiveskull
www.OpenSubtitles.org

